# Vercel's zero-config "Other" preset (no framework detected) serves every
# file in this project at its literal repo path unless it's ignored here or
# lives under api/ (which becomes serverless functions instead). That means
# without this file, things like scripts/test-attio.js or .env.example would
# be publicly readable at https://your-deployment.vercel.app/scripts/test-attio.js
# etc. None of these contain real secrets (see lib/config.js's own header
# comment — nothing in the source is ever a real key), but they're
# developer-only tooling with no reason to be public.
#
# Do NOT add lib/ here — api/*.js requires('../lib/...') at runtime, and
# ignoring it here would remove it from the deployment entirely, breaking
# every endpoint.

scripts/
.env.example
*.png

# preview.html / index.html are the local, double-click-to-open demo page
# (built by scripts/build-preview.js) that fakes every form submission on
# purpose, so the widget can be clicked around with no backend running.
# They must NOT be deployed: because Vercel serves index.html at the site
# root by default, leaving this in meant the LIVE production URL was
# silently serving the mocked demo instead of a real page — anyone testing
# by visiting that URL directly got a fake "Sent" response with no email,
# no Attio write, and no server-side request at all, which is exactly what
# happened during a real test. Nothing needs to be served at the production
# root anyway (RentCafe only ever loads /widget.js and calls /api/*), so a
# 404 there after this change is correct, expected behavior.
preview.html
index.html
